IMPORT prelude

-- Application of English Law Act 1993 (Singapore) -- which English law is Singapore law: the common law and equity (s 3), the
-- English statutes listed in the First Schedule and the extent of each (s 4(1), (2) and Parts 1 and 2 of the First Schedule),
-- the priority of local Acts (s 4(3)), how references in a listed statute are read (s 4(4)), the closing rule (s 5(1)), the
-- transitional saving of the old Civil Law Act s 5 (s 6(2)), and four of the rules the Second Schedule wrote into other Acts:
-- Civil Law Act s 6A (contracts that must be evidenced in writing), Conveyancing and Law of Property Act s 18A (relief against
-- forfeiture for non-payment of rent), and Insurance Act ss 61A and 61B (insurable interest; accidental fire).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/AELA1993.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates
-- all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The latest amendment
-- annotated in the text is [4/2021] (Act 4 of 2021, the First Schedule Part 3 amendments and the deletion of Part 1 item 1).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0043 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. For this Act the honest answer is: which English contract and commercial statutes bind them,
-- and to what extent.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 5(2) (Interpretation Act 1965 on a cesser, stated not modelled); s 6(1), (3) (repeals, spent); s 7; s 8
-- (Minister's modification orders -- none was retrieved); s 9 (revised editions of English enactments); First Schedule Part 3
-- (textual amendments to the listed statutes, read but not modelled); the Second Schedule's other insertions (Civil Law Act
-- ss 4(2A), (2B) voluntary waste, 6B trusts of land in writing, 16A chain of executorship; CLPA s 69A accumulations, s 73A
-- co-owner's account, ss 73B, 73C conveyances to defraud creditors or purchasers; Extradition Act s 43; Penal Code ss 130B,
-- 130C piracy). The Second Schedule rules encoded here are AS INSERTED IN 1993; their present text in the Civil Law Act, the
-- CLPA and the Insurance Act was NOT checked and may have been renumbered or amended since.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Application of English Law Act 1993`

§§ `2 and First Schedule -- the English enactments`

-- s 2: "English enactment" means an enactment of the Parliament of England, of Great Britain or of the United Kingdom.
-- First Schedule Part 1 (Imperial Acts): item 1 "[Deleted by Act 4 of 2021]"; 2. Maritime Conventions Act 1911; 3. Straits
-- Settlements and Johore Territorial Waters (Agreement) Act 1928. Part 2 (commercial law): Mercantile Law Amendment Act 1856,
-- Policies of Assurance Act 1867, Factors Act 1889, Partnership Act 1890, Marine Insurance Act 1906, Third Parties (Rights
-- against Insurers) Act 1930, Corporate Bodies' Contracts Act 1960, Misrepresentation Act 1967, Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977,
-- Sale of Goods Act 1979, Supply of Goods and Services Act 1982, Minors' Contracts Act 1987, Carriage of Goods by Sea Act 1992.
-- The last four in the list below are NOT in the Schedule; they are here to test the closing rule.
DECLARE EnglishEnactment IS ONE OF
    `the Maritime Conventions Act 1911`
    `the Straits Settlements and Johore Territorial Waters (Agreement) Act 1928`
    `the Mercantile Law Amendment Act 1856`
    `the Policies of Assurance Act 1867`
    `the Factors Act 1889`
    `the Partnership Act 1890`
    `the Marine Insurance Act 1906`
    `the Third Parties (Rights against Insurers) Act 1930`
    `the Corporate Bodies' Contracts Act 1960`
    `the Misrepresentation Act 1967`
    `the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977`
    `the Sale of Goods Act 1979`
    `the Supply of Goods and Services Act 1982`
    `the Minors' Contracts Act 1987`
    `the Carriage of Goods by Sea Act 1992`
    `the Statute of Frauds 1677`
    `the Law of Property Act 1925`
    `the Life Assurance Act 1774`
    `the Consumer Rights Act 2015`

GIVEN `the enactment` IS AN EnglishEnactment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the First Schedule Part listing it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the enactment`
    WHEN `the Maritime Conventions Act 1911` THEN 1
    WHEN `the Straits Settlements and Johore Territorial Waters (Agreement) Act 1928` THEN 1
    WHEN `the Mercantile Law Amendment Act 1856` THEN 2
    WHEN `the Policies of Assurance Act 1867` THEN 2
    WHEN `the Factors Act 1889` THEN 2
    WHEN `the Partnership Act 1890` THEN 2
    WHEN `the Marine Insurance Act 1906` THEN 2
    WHEN `the Third Parties (Rights against Insurers) Act 1930` THEN 2
    WHEN `the Corporate Bodies' Contracts Act 1960` THEN 2
    WHEN `the Misrepresentation Act 1967` THEN 2
    WHEN `the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977` THEN 2
    WHEN `the Sale of Goods Act 1979` THEN 2
    WHEN `the Supply of Goods and Services Act 1982` THEN 2
    WHEN `the Minors' Contracts Act 1987` THEN 2
    WHEN `the Carriage of Goods by Sea Act 1992` THEN 2
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `4(1) and 5(1) -- does an English enactment apply at all`

-- s 4(1): "Subject to the provisions of this section and of any other written law, the following English enactments, with the
-- necessary modifications, apply or continue to apply in Singapore: (a) the English enactments specified in ... the First
-- Schedule to the extent specified in the fourth column thereof; and (b) any other English enactment which applies to or is in
-- force in Singapore by virtue of any written law."
-- s 5(1): "Except as provided in this Act, no English enactment is part of the law of Singapore."
GIVEN `the enactment` IS AN EnglishEnactment, `applied by another written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the enactment applies in Singapore` IF
        `the First Schedule Part listing it` `the enactment` GREATER THAN 0
    OR  `applied by another written law`

§§ `4(1)(a), 4(2) and First Schedule column 4 -- which provisions of a listed enactment apply`

-- s 4(2): "The English enactments specified in Part 2 of the First Schedule are the enactments as they are in force as at
-- 12 November 1993, subject to the exceptions specified in the fourth column of that Part and to the amendments specified in
-- Part 3 of that Schedule." s 4(2) says nothing about Part 1, so for a Part 1 enactment this encoding does not exclude later
-- UK text; that is a default, not something the text decides.
-- Fourth column: Mercantile Law Amendment Act 1856 "Sections 3 and 5". Policies of Assurance Act 1867 "The whole except
-- section 8". Factors Act 1889 "The whole except the amendment to section 9 by the Consumer Credit Act 1974". Third Parties
-- (Rights against Insurers) Act 1930 "The whole except the amendments effected by the Insolvency Act 1985 and the Insolvency
-- Act 1986". Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 "Part I (except section 1(1)(c) and (3)(b) and the amendment to that section by
-- the Occupiers' Liability Act 1984) and Part III". Sale of Goods Act 1979 "The whole except sections 22 and 25(2)". Supply of
-- Goods and Services Act 1982 "The whole except Part II". Minors' Contracts Act 1987 "The whole except sections 1(b) and 4(1)".
-- All others "The whole".
DECLARE TextOrigin IS ONE OF
    `original text`
    `the amendment by the Consumer Credit Act 1974`
    `the amendment by the Insolvency Act 1985`
    `the amendment by the Insolvency Act 1986`
    `the amendment by the Occupiers' Liability Act 1984`
    `a UK amendment made after 12 November 1993`

-- A provision is identified down to the smallest unit asked about. `subsection` 0 and `paragraph` "" mean "not a particular
-- subsection / paragraph". A question about a whole section that is only partly excepted is answered as applying.
DECLARE Provision HAS
    `enactment`   IS AN EnglishEnactment
    `part`        IS A NUMBER
    `section`     IS A NUMBER
    `subsection`  IS A NUMBER
    `paragraph`   IS A STRING
    `text origin` IS A TextOrigin

GIVEN `the provision` IS A Provision, `s` IS A NUMBER, `ss` IS A NUMBER, `para` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision falls within` IF
        `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS `s`
    AND (`ss` EQUALS 0 OR `the provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS `ss`)
    AND (`para` EQUALS "" OR `the provision`'s `paragraph` EQUALS `para`)

GIVEN `the origin` IS A TextOrigin
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the text is a post-1993 UK amendment` IF
    CONSIDER `the origin`
    WHEN `a UK amendment made after 12 November 1993` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the origin` IS A TextOrigin
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the text is the Consumer Credit Act 1974 amendment` IF
    CONSIDER `the origin`
    WHEN `the amendment by the Consumer Credit Act 1974` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the origin` IS A TextOrigin
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the text is an Insolvency Act amendment` IF
    CONSIDER `the origin`
    WHEN `the amendment by the Insolvency Act 1985` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the amendment by the Insolvency Act 1986` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the origin` IS A TextOrigin
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the text is the Occupiers' Liability Act 1984 amendment` IF
    CONSIDER `the origin`
    WHEN `the amendment by the Occupiers' Liability Act 1984` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the provision` IS A Provision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the UCTA provision is within the extent` IF
        (    `the provision`'s `part` EQUALS 1
         AND (NOT `the provision falls within` `the provision` 1 1 "c")
         AND (NOT `the provision falls within` `the provision` 1 3 "b")
         AND (NOT (`the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 1 AND `the text is the Occupiers' Liability Act 1984 amendment` (`the provision`'s `text origin`))))
    OR  `the provision`'s `part` EQUALS 3

GIVEN `the provision` IS A Provision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision is within the fourth column` IF
    CONSIDER `the provision`'s `enactment`
    WHEN `the Maritime Conventions Act 1911` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Straits Settlements and Johore Territorial Waters (Agreement) Act 1928` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Mercantile Law Amendment Act 1856` THEN `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 3 OR `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 5
    WHEN `the Policies of Assurance Act 1867` THEN NOT (`the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 8)
    WHEN `the Factors Act 1889` THEN NOT (`the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 9 AND `the text is the Consumer Credit Act 1974 amendment` (`the provision`'s `text origin`))
    WHEN `the Partnership Act 1890` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Marine Insurance Act 1906` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Third Parties (Rights against Insurers) Act 1930` THEN NOT `the text is an Insolvency Act amendment` (`the provision`'s `text origin`)
    WHEN `the Corporate Bodies' Contracts Act 1960` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Misrepresentation Act 1967` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977` THEN `the UCTA provision is within the extent` `the provision`
    WHEN `the Sale of Goods Act 1979` THEN (NOT (`the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 22)) AND (NOT `the provision falls within` `the provision` 25 2 "")
    WHEN `the Supply of Goods and Services Act 1982` THEN NOT (`the provision`'s `part` EQUALS 2)
    WHEN `the Minors' Contracts Act 1987` THEN (NOT `the provision falls within` `the provision` 1 0 "b") AND (NOT `the provision falls within` `the provision` 4 1 "")
    WHEN `the Carriage of Goods by Sea Act 1992` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the provision` IS A Provision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision applies in Singapore` IF
        `the provision is within the fourth column` `the provision`
    AND (NOT (    `the First Schedule Part listing it` (`the provision`'s `enactment`) EQUALS 2
              AND `the text is a post-1993 UK amendment` (`the provision`'s `text origin`)))

§§ `4(3) -- local Acts prevail`

-- s 4(3): "To the extent to which any of the provisions of any English enactment is inconsistent with the provisions of any
-- local Act in force at or after 12 November 1993, the provisions of the local Act prevail." s 2: "local Act" includes any
-- Ordinance or Act of Singapore or of Malaysia having the force of law in Singapore.
GIVEN `the provision` IS A Provision, `inconsistent with a local Act in force at or after 12 November 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the English provision governs` IF
        `the provision applies in Singapore` `the provision`
    AND (NOT `inconsistent with a local Act in force at or after 12 November 1993`)

§§ `4(4) -- reading a listed enactment in Singapore`

-- s 4(4): in a First Schedule enactment, unless the context otherwise requires, "(a) any reference to the United Kingdom is to be
-- read as a reference to Singapore; (b) ... the High Court ... the General Division of the High Court in Singapore; (c) ... a
-- County Court ... a District Court in Singapore; (d) ... the holder of an office ... the holder of the corresponding office in
-- Singapore; (e) ... a statute or a statutory provision ... the corresponding statute or statutory provision in Singapore; and
-- (f) any reference or provision relating to Scotland or Northern Ireland ... is to be disregarded." [40/2019]
DECLARE Reference IS ONE OF
    `the United Kingdom`
    `the High Court`
    `a County Court`
    `a UK office holder`
    `a UK statute`
    `Scotland`
    `Northern Ireland`

GIVEN `the reference` IS A Reference
GIVETH A STRING
`how the reference is read` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reference`
    WHEN `the United Kingdom` THEN "Singapore"
    WHEN `the High Court` THEN "the General Division of the High Court in Singapore"
    WHEN `a County Court` THEN "a District Court in Singapore"
    WHEN `a UK office holder` THEN "the holder of the corresponding office in Singapore"
    WHEN `a UK statute` THEN "the corresponding statute or statutory provision in Singapore"
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN "disregarded"
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN "disregarded"

§§ `3 -- the common law of England and equity`

-- s 3(1): "The common law of England (including the principles and rules of equity), so far as it was part of the law of
-- Singapore immediately before 12 November 1993, continues to be part of the law of Singapore." (2): "so far as it is
-- applicable to the circumstances of Singapore and its inhabitants and subject to such modifications as those circumstances
-- may require." A rule of equity is treated exactly like a rule of common law, so equity is not a separate input.
GIVEN `part of Singapore law immediately before 12 November 1993` IS A BOOLEAN, `applicable to the circumstances of Singapore and its inhabitants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the English common law rule continues in Singapore` IF
        `part of Singapore law immediately before 12 November 1993`
    AND `applicable to the circumstances of Singapore and its inhabitants`

§§ `6(2) -- the old Civil Law Act s 5 survives for old claims`

-- s 6(1): section 5 of the Civil Law Act (Cap. 43, 1988 Revised Edition) is repealed. (2): "In respect of any proceedings
-- instituted or any cause of action accruing before 12 November 1993, section 5 of the Civil Law Act ... continues to apply as
-- if it had not been repealed by this Act."
GIVEN `proceedings instituted before 12 November 1993` IS A BOOLEAN, `cause of action accrued before 12 November 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the old Civil Law Act s 5 still applies` IF
        `proceedings instituted before 12 November 1993`
    OR  `cause of action accrued before 12 November 1993`

§§ `Second Schedule para 1(b) -- Civil Law Act s 6A, contracts to be evidenced in writing`

-- s 6A (as inserted): "No action shall be brought against -- (a) any executor or administrator upon any special promise to
-- answer damages out of his own estate; (b) any defendant upon any special promise to answer for the debt, default or
-- miscarriage of another person; (c) any person upon any agreement made upon consideration of marriage; (d) any person upon any
-- contract for the sale or other disposition of immovable property, or any interest in such property; or (e) any person upon
-- any agreement that is not to be performed within the space of one year from the making thereof, unless the promise or
-- agreement ... or some memorandum or note thereof, is in writing and signed by the party to be charged therewith or some other
-- person lawfully authorised by him."
DECLARE Promise IS ONE OF
    `an executor's promise to pay damages out of his own estate`
    `a guarantee of another person's debt`
    `an agreement made in consideration of marriage`
    `a contract to sell land`
    `a three-year consultancy agreement`
    `a contract to sell a used car`
    `a six-month tenancy of a flat`

GIVEN `the promise` IS A Promise
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the promise needs signed writing` IF
    CONSIDER `the promise`
    WHEN `an executor's promise to pay damages out of his own estate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a guarantee of another person's debt` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an agreement made in consideration of marriage` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a contract to sell land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a three-year consultancy agreement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a six-month tenancy of a flat` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the promise` IS A Promise, `signed writing by the party charged or his authorised agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action can be brought on the promise` IF
        (NOT `the promise needs signed writing` `the promise`)
    OR  `signed writing by the party charged or his authorised agent`

§§ `Second Schedule para 2(a) -- CLPA s 18A, relief against forfeiture for non-payment of rent`

-- s 18A(2) (as inserted): if, within the time prescribed by rules of court for acknowledging service of the writ, "the lessee
-- pays into court all the rent in arrear and the costs of the action, the action shall cease, and the lessee shall hold the land
-- according to the lease without any new lease." (6): "Subsection (2) shall not apply where the lessor is proceeding in the same
-- action to enforce a right of re-entry or forfeiture on any other ground as well as for non-payment of rent, or to enforce any
-- other claim as well ..." (3): otherwise the court orders possession "at the expiration of such period, but not being less than
-- 4 weeks from the date of the order", unless the lessee pays arrears and the costs directed; (4) the period may be extended
-- before possession is recovered; (5) payment within the period or extended period: the lessee holds under the lease; (7)
-- otherwise "the lessee shall be barred from all relief".
GIVEN `paid arrears and costs into court within the time for acknowledging service` IS A BOOLEAN, `lessor also sues on another ground or another claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the forfeiture action ceases` IF
        `paid arrears and costs into court within the time for acknowledging service`
    AND (NOT `lessor also sues on another ground or another claim`)

GIVEN `weeks from the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the possession period is permitted` IF
    `weeks from the order` AT LEAST 4

GIVEN `paid arrears and costs into court within the time for acknowledging service` IS A BOOLEAN, `lessor also sues on another ground or another claim` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid arrears and directed costs within the ordered or extended period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessee keeps the lease` IF
        `the forfeiture action ceases` `paid arrears and costs into court within the time for acknowledging service` `lessor also sues on another ground or another claim`
    OR  `paid arrears and directed costs within the ordered or extended period`

§§ `Second Schedule para 4 -- Insurance Act ss 61A and 61B`

-- s 61A(1) (as inserted): "No insurance shall be made by any person on any event wherein the person for whose use or benefit
-- or on whose account the policy is made has no interest, or by way of gaming or wagering; and every assurance made contrary to
-- this subsection shall be void." (3): "In all cases where there is an interest in such event, no greater sum shall be recovered
-- or received from the insurer than the amount or value of the interest." (4): "Nothing in this section shall extend to
-- insurance made by any person on ships or goods, or to contracts of indemnity against loss by fire or loss by other events
-- whatsoever." (2), the duty to insert the names of the persons interested, is not encoded.
GIVEN `the beneficiary has an interest in the event` IS A BOOLEAN, `by way of gaming or wagering` IS A BOOLEAN, `on ships or goods or an indemnity contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insurance is void` IF
        (NOT `on ships or goods or an indemnity contract`)
    AND ((NOT `the beneficiary has an interest in the event`) OR `by way of gaming or wagering`)

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- Where s 61A(4) applies the section imposes no cap; any cap from the general law of indemnity is outside this encoding, so the
-- sum insured is returned.
GIVEN `sum insured` IS A NUMBER, `value of the interest` IS A NUMBER, `on ships or goods or an indemnity contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most recoverable under s 61A` MEANS
    IF `on ships or goods or an indemnity contract`
    THEN `sum insured`
    ELSE `the lesser of` `sum insured` `value of the interest`

-- s 61B (as inserted): "No action shall lie against a person in whose house or premises or on whose estate any fire accidentally
-- began except that no contract or agreement made between landlord and tenant shall be hereby defeated or made void."
GIVEN `the fire began accidentally on the defendant's premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `sued on a landlord-tenant contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action lies over the fire` IF
        (NOT `the fire began accidentally on the defendant's premises`)
    OR  `sued on a landlord-tenant contract`
